```

At least all examples could be updated with this.

Since BusObject is a public interface, I'm not inclined to break it by adding an additional method requirement. Another way to handle this is to add something like:
```
type conner interface {
     Conn() *Conn
}

func BusObjectConn(bo BusObject) (*Conn, error) {
    c, ok := bo.(conner)
    if !ok {
        return nil, errors.New("cannot get conn")
    }
    return c.Conn(), nil
}
